{"id": "unknown-2026-10-03-009", "date": "2026-10-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["coking_coal_scrap", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s steel boom is reshaping the global trade in coking coal and coke — Argus", "content": "<p>The boom in India’s steel industry is transforming the global market for the seaborne transport of metallurgical coal and coke  Argus reports this. According to industry analysts, steel production in India has risen from 104 million tonnes in 2021 to approximately 169 million tonnes in 2026. Meanwhile, installed capacity has reached around 220 million tonnes, [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://gmk.center/en/news/india-s-steel-boom-is-reshaping-the-global-trade-in-coking-coal-and-coke-", "sources": [{"name": "gmk_center", "url": "https://gmk.center/en/news/india-s-steel-boom-is-reshaping-the-global-trade-in-coking-coal-and-coke-argus/", "type": "rss"}]}
